# Job: dotnet framework — ClientServer Server-only topology reports Degraded/IsReady=false although it serves (perf phase 1 B1)

You are a codex sub-agent under a Claude supervisor. Model gpt-6-astra, reasoning xhigh. Cap 2 h. Read `AGENTS.md` §2/§3/§4.1/§5, `framework/AGENTS.md`, `framework/languages/dotnet/AGENTS.md` if present. Campaign rules: no mitigations, one owner per rule, fewer rules, public API unchanged, regression test per fix, cross-language parity mandatory. Never modify `core/**`, `bindings/**`, any `doc/spec/**`, `framework/doc/**`, `doc/site/**`, other languages' runtime (read them for parity). Do not commit. dotnet env: `source framework/languages/dotnet/perf/scripts/dotnet-env.sh` or the gate env block (TMPDIR=/dev/shm/zlink-tmp-dotnet, ZLINK_LIBRARY_PATH=core/build-dev/lib, NUGET_PACKAGES hash dir); take `/tmp/zlink-dotnet-gate.lock` (flock) for builds/tests and `/tmp/zlink-samples-gate.lock` for samples. Another job runs perf diagnostics in `framework/languages/dotnet/perf` — do not edit perf/.

## Defect (supervisor-verified)
`framework/languages/dotnet/src/Zlink.Framework/Runtime/Channels/ZLinkClientServerRuntimeService.cs:98` builds `Selectable: state.HasClient && _runtime.IsStarted && readyCount > 0` and `:131` projects public `IsReady` from it. A process registered only as ClientServer Server (manual topology, target Ready, weight 100, host Serving) therefore reports topology `Degraded`, `IsReady=false`, while it processes typed requests. Spec: `framework/doc/framework/common/spec/server/06-observability/01-runtime-monitoring.ko.md:194` — `ready` = host serving and the topology can process application messages; `languages/dotnet/interfaces/10-topology-monitoring.ko.md:359-379` (`IsReady`, `ReadyTargetCount` includes local/remote Ready Servers). Evidence: `doc/plan/c016-worklog/perf-dotnet-runner-phase1-summary.md` §BLOCKERS B1 (public repro with two processes).

## Task
1. Separate the two judgments that `Selectable` conflates: "this process can select a target for outbound calls" (needs a Client role and a ready target) vs. "this topology is ready" (host Serving, runtime started, and — for Server role — the local server is registered/listening and Ready; for Client role — at least one ready target). One owner for each; do not add a third state. Keep `Selectable` for the outbound selection path if it is used there.
2. Cross-language: read java (`ZLinkTopologyRuntimeViews.java`, `ZLinkChannelRuntime.java:1035/1077` hasClientRegistration), node (`runtime/channels/*` client-server status projection) and cpp for how a Server-only ClientServer status is projected. If they share the defect, report the exact lines (do not edit them); if they are correct, cite them as the reference.
3. Regression test (dotnet unit): Server-only ClientServer host → `GetStatus` is `Ready`, `IsReady=true`, `ReadyTargetCount=1`; Client-only with no ready target → not ready; Client+Server unchanged.
4. Gate: unit tests (`dotnet test tests/Zlink.Framework.UnitTests` split as the gate does), SampleRegression, and the 7 samples via `samples/run_samples.sh` under the locks. 0 failures.

